                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Cute and aesthetically pleasing rhythm game that is fairly beginner friendly.\r\n I cannot play rhythm games for the life of me because I simply suck ass at them. Whereas normally I am inclined to get frustrated and give up, Melatonin does provide you with multiple game modes per level to help you get used to the rhythm and the mechanics. Every level is different, though they all have the same cutesy aesthetic and sound design (with different songs and sounds of course). This is a rare instance in which a rhythm game is enjoyable to try hard and get better at, even if you're absolutely hopeless musically. :)",
